# catalog/lane-run-inputs.d/alerts-medic.rw — the per-project files one
# `bin/alerts-medic.sh $p` run writes. A write-back may carry these only. The ro
# snapshot is these plus alerts-medic.ro. The inventory, with file:line for each
# entry, is in docs/notes/2026-10-14-BH-6720-llm-alert-lanes-offhub.md.
#
# NOT CARRIED. A project run also writes these fleet-wide files, and they
# block a flip of alerts-medic to Fly:
#   logs/ALERTS.log (appends, bin/alerts-medic.sh:384,691,705,762)
#   logs/medic.log (every project run appends to one log, bin/alerts-medic.sh:53;
#     the lane log that rides back is logs/alerts-medic.log)
#   flags/alerted-medic-*, flags/lane-caps-degraded-*, logs/lane-caps.log,
#   logs/model-route.log, logs/cost.csv
# The shared seeds state/medic-seen.txt, state/medic-families.json and
# state/medic-parked.json (bin/alerts-medic.sh:133-139) are read only when the
# project's own copy is absent, and the project's copy rides below.
# bin/alerts-medic.sh:19 sets HARNESS=/root/harness with no condition.
# Secrets, locks and machine-local caches are never carried: env/*, locks/*,
# state/gh-*, state/settings-cache.json, state/lane-gate/*.
#
# medic-seen.txt, medic-families.json, medic-parked.json
# (bin/alerts-medic.sh:132,346-347,813-814,830,846)
state/alerts-medic/$p/**
# bin/alerts-medic.sh:725-726,791
logs/medic-run.$p.txt
